tication & credentials:\\n  - Use built-in credential types (API Key, OAuth2, Basic Auth).\\n  - Store credentials centrally and reference them in nodes.\\n- Pagination & rate limits:\\n  - Use pagination settings or loop with SplitInBatches/Continue while handling next-page tokens.\\n  - Add Wait nodes or rate-limit logic when APIs impose limits.\\n- Error handling & retries:\\n  - Use Error Trigger, \\\"Continue On Fail\\\" in node settings, and manual try/catch in Function nodes.\\n  - Set workflow-level or node-level retry/backoff strategies.\\n- Testing & debugging:\\n  - Execute single nodes, inspect input/output, use “Execute Workflow” and check node run data.\\n  - Use console.log in Function nodes; check execution logs.\\n- Best practices:\\n  - Keep workflows modular, use sub-workflows (Execute Workflow).\\n  - Name nodes clearly and comment complex expression logic.\\n  - Limit sensitive data exposure; use credentials properly.\\n  - Use environment variables for endpoints/keys in different environments.\\n- Useful shortcuts & tips:\\n  - Duplicate nodes, connect/disconnect with drag-and-drop.\\n  - Use Merge/Wait/IF to control flow; use Set to shape payloads before API calls.\\n  - Use node “Run Once” or “Run All” depending on test scope.\\n\\nTell me if you want:\\n- A precise summary of your uploaded cheat sheet (please attach it), or\\n- A longer walkthrough with examples for any of the bullets above.\",\"generationInfo\":{\"prompt\":0,\"completion\":0,\"finish_reason\":\"stop\",\"system_fingerprint\":null,\"model_name\":\"gpt-5-mini-2025-08-07\"}}]]},\"tokenUsage\":{\"completionTokens\":915,\"promptTokens\":178,\"totalTokens\":1093}}}"}}
